# Windows batch launchers must keep CRLF line endings.
#
# cmd.exe reads a .cmd/.bat file by BYTE OFFSET, so an LF-only script can make
# it resume mid-line -- labels (goto) resolve wrongly and fragments of the
# file get executed as commands. Pin the endings here instead of relying on
# each machine's core.autocrlf setting.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
